.TH LIGHTDDNS 1 "2026" "lightddns" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lightddns \- lightweight dynamic DNS updater
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lightddns
[\fB\-D\fR \fIworkdir\fR] [\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIfile\fR]
.IR command " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lightddns
watches an IP through a datasource and pushes changes to a DNS provider.
Configuration is a YAML file (a Go template exposing \fB{{ .Env.KEY }}\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \-c \fIfile\fR
Start the updater daemon.
.TP
.B check \-c \fIfile\fR
Validate a configuration file and exit.
.TP
.B version
Print version information.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-workdir " \fIdir\fR"
Working directory. Relative \fB\-c\fR paths resolve against it; absolute ones
are read directly.
.TP
.B \-\-env\-file " \fIfile\fR"
Load KEY=VALUE pairs from \fIfile\fR into the environment. Without it only the
inherited environment is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lightddns.yaml
Main configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/lightddns.d/*.yaml
Per-instance configs, run via \fBlightddns@\fIname\fR\fB.service\fR.
.TP
.I /etc/default/lightddns
Environment / secrets and the optional \fBARG\fR override.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Full documentation at
.UR https://lightddns.duaky.com
.UE .